usage: control.py [-h] [--samples SAMPLES] [--interval INTERVAL] [--edge]
                  [--threshold THRESHOLD]
                  [--view {color,gray,edge,compare,denoise,overlay,reference}]
                  [--frame {live,freeze,step,record,play,pause,next,reference,clear-reference}]
                  [--set R G B GAMMA PHASE] [--algorithm {sobel,canny}]
                  [--low-ratio {1/4,1/2,3/4}] [--median {on,off}]
                  [--recognition {on,off}] [--sensor-status]
                  [--exposure-half-lines EXPOSURE_HALF_LINES | --exposure-ms EXPOSURE_MS]
                  [--sensor-gain {1,2,3}] [--sensor-save SENSOR_SAVE]
                  [--sensor-restore SENSOR_RESTORE]

Read the full-field camera and set its Bayer phase or white balance.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --samples SAMPLES
  --interval INTERVAL
  --edge                Use the edge-system project
  --threshold THRESHOLD
                        Threshold: Sobel 0..2040, Canny 1..2040
  --view {color,gray,edge,compare,denoise,overlay,reference}
                        Edge display mode; keeps active gains
  --frame {live,freeze,step,record,play,pause,next,reference,clear-reference}
                        Frame operation; record explicitly replaces the
                        32-frame clip
  --set R G B GAMMA PHASE
                        Q8.8 gains (256=1x), gamma 0/1, Bayer phase 0..3
  --algorithm {sobel,canny}
                        Frame-committed edge algorithm
  --low-ratio {1/4,1/2,3/4}
                        Canny low/high threshold ratio
  --median {on,off}     Frame-committed median filter
  --recognition {on,off}
                        Frame-committed circle/rectangle recognition
  --sensor-status       Read O1 sensor timing, exposure and gain
  --exposure-half-lines EXPOSURE_HALF_LINES
                        SC431HAI manual exposure in half-lines
  --exposure-ms EXPOSURE_MS
                        Exposure in ms, calibrated from measured capture FPS
  --sensor-gain {1,2,3}
                        Analog gain 1x, 2.021x or 3.032x; digital gain stays
                        1x
  --sensor-save SENSOR_SAVE
                        Save sensor registers to a new JSON file
  --sensor-restore SENSOR_RESTORE
                        Restore exposure/gain from a saved O1 JSON file
